# Dastro 3.1 — manual patch

## 1. Add the DatoCMS CLI as a dev dependency

Every dastro project should have the official DatoCMS CLI available locally so
schema migrations, `schema:inspect`, `cma:call` and environment operations run
the same way in each project and in CI.

```sh
npm i -D datocms@latest
```

## 2. Add `datocms.config.json`

If the file does not exist yet, create it next to `package.json` with exactly
this content:

```json
{
  "profiles": {
    "default": {
      "apiTokenEnvName": "DATO_CMS_CMA_TOKEN",
      "logLevel": "BASIC"
    }
  }
}
```

The CLI then authenticates with the `DATO_CMS_CMA_TOKEN` already in your `.env`
(and in CI), so no `datocms login` or `datocms link` is needed. Commit the
file — it contains no tokens.

## 3. Sync the managed `AGENTS.md` section

Dastro now ships its agent doc at
`node_modules/dastro/consumer-docs/agents/CONSUMER-AGENTS.md`. Upgrades from an
older dastro CLI still look for `node_modules/dastro/AGENTS.md`, so this sync
was skipped. Replace the block between `<!-- @dastro:managed -->` and
`<!-- @dastro:managed:end -->` in your `AGENTS.md` with the same block from
`CONSUMER-AGENTS.md` (or copy the whole file if `AGENTS.md` does not exist).
Later upgrades sync it automatically.

## 4. Remove the boilerplate-specific section from `AGENTS.md`

If `AGENTS.md` has a `## Boilerplate-specific` section (e.g. "Gridonic headless
website boilerplate. Local dev server runs at `https://localhost:4321`"),
delete it: from that heading up to, but not including, the next `## ` heading
(or end of file if none follows).

## 5. Add agent skill docs

Copy these files from `node_modules/dastro/consumer-docs/agents/` into
`docs/agents/`, skipping any that already exist:

- `domain.md`
- `issue-tracker.md`
- `triage-labels.md`

If `AGENTS.md` has no `## Agent skills` section yet, append the following,
replacing `<owner>/<repo>` with the GitHub repo from `git remote -v`:

```md

## Agent skills

### Issue tracker

GitHub Issues  via `gh` CLI. See `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`.

### Triage labels

Default canonical labels (`needs-triage`, `needs-info`, `ready-for-agent`, `ready-for-human`, `wontfix`). See `docs/agents/triage-labels.md`.

### Domain docs

Single-context: root `CONTEXT.md` + `docs/adr/`. See `docs/agents/domain.md`.
```

## 6. Add a `## Links` section to `AGENTS.md`

If `AGENTS.md` has no `## Links` section yet, append one as the last section:
a table of project links, one row per link, each labelled by what it is.

Discover links from the project itself. Sources, in order:

- `README.md` (the `## Links` table and any other project URLs)
- `git remote -v` → GitHub repo
- `.netlify/state.json` `siteId` or `netlify status` → Netlify site and
  production / preview URLs
- `.env` / `datocms.config.json` / `npx datocms cma:call site find` → DatoCMS
  admin URL (never copy tokens)
- Boilerplate Radar (https://boilerplate-radar.gridonic.io) → instances, CMS
- Figma, prototype (`prototype.gridonic.io`), scoping board, Jira / Confluence
  URLs found in the repo, open issues, or PR descriptions

Include only links you found and verified; omit a category rather than
guessing. Example shape:

```md
## Links

| What          | URL                                   |
|---------------|---------------------------------------|
| Production    | https://example.ch                    |
| DatoCMS       | https://example.admin.datocms.com     |
| GitHub        | https://github.com/gridonic/example   |
| Netlify       | https://app.netlify.com/projects/example |
| Prototype     | https://prototype.gridonic.io/example |
| Scoping board | https://…                             |
```

## 7. Refactor `className` props to `class` (if necessary)

Astro 7 compiles `.astro` files with the Rust compiler, which adds the parent's
scope class (`astro-xxxx`) only to `class` on components, no longer to
`className`. So when a parent passes `className="…"` to a child component
**and** styles that class in its scoped `<style>`, those styles silently stop
applying.

Find component `className` usages, including multi-line tags and
`className={…}`, plus `className` in child `Props`:

```sh
grep -rnE 'className(=|\?:|:)' src --include='*.astro'
```

Refactor each one where the parent's scoped styles target the class. Skip
it if they don't:

- Child: `const { class: className } = Astro.props;` and `class?: string` in
  `interface Props`.
- Parent: pass `class="…"` instead of `className="…"`.

Don't use `:global()` in the parent as a workaround. Afterwards, compare the
affected modules against production.
